hey guys it's Jan here Tom Hardy gives a  dazzling double performance as twin East  and gangsters Reggie and Ronnie Kray in  the true crime drama legend as Reggie  Hardy is ostensibly all smooth surfaces  and rounded edges a charming veneer that  masks a propensity for ferocious  violence as Ronnie Hardy can go from  quietly spoken candor and Menace to  snarling spitting indignation and  psychopathic rage in the blink of an eye  but even in those quieter moments we  always know that Ronnie is looking for  his next showdown  even without the character's physical  differences Hardy puts in such a strong  turn as each brother that you'd have no  problem telling them apart and the way  the brothers are presented on screen  isn't all about cunning camera  positioning and actor doubles in fact we  often see Hardy as both Reggie and  Ronnie on screen side-by-side in the  same shot of course Hardy's not  the first actor to take on twin roles in  a movie there was army hammer in the  social network Freddie Highmore and  Spiderwick Chronicles and of course  Jeremy Irons in Dead Ringers just to  name a few  and it's not the first time that  Hardee's brought a real-life criminal to  life on the big screen either remember  Drive director Nicolas Winding reckons  super stylized film Bronson back in 2009  when it featured Heidi giving an  insanely bold turn as Britain's most  dangerous prisoner Charles Bronson and  of course Hardy's also made in number of  frames in the crime drama genre already  most recently he played Jewish gang  leader Alfie Solomon's in the BBC period  crime drama peaky blinders and before  that he starred in the fantastic crime  dramas the drop and lawless and then  there was of course layer cake and  RocknRolla too of course none of that  negates what a stellar performance tom  hardy gives in this movie legend as for  the supporting cast well as Reggie's  girlfriends and later wife we've got  sucker punch star Emily Browning and her  delicate features and softly spoken  approach of occasional quiet defiance  works well and on top of that she looks  tiny next to Tom Hardy which makes  Reggie and Ronnie seem even more in  posing in intimidating there's also a  whole raft of brilliant British actors  in supporting roles though some feel  underused given their talent still  that's to be expected as legend is  obviously the Ronnie and Reggie show and  therefore very much the Tom Hardy show  Harry Potter's David Thewlis puts in a  neat turn as a crazed accountant also  look out for Kingsman the Secret Service  star Taron Egerton as Ronnie's lover  Teddy former doctor whose star  Christopher Eccleston as a policeman  after the crazed Paul Bettany is a rival  gang leader and Hardy's peaky blinders  co-star Paul Anderson as one of the  crave gang by the way we'll see Anderson  join Hardy on-screen again shortly in  Gonzales in Yeley twos the revenant and  there's Merlin star Colin Morgan who  plays Francis's brother who's also  Reggie's driver Morgan continues to show  real promise as a film actor and it's  obvious he just needs the right breakout  part now to make a bigger name for  himself in movies legends writer  director Brian Helgeland is best known  for writing loads of screenplays  including the superb LA Confidential  though he's also directed a number of  films such as baseball biopic 42 and the  Knight's Tale starring Heath Ledger  helgeland based this film on author John  Pearson's non-fiction book the  profession of violence the rise and fall  of the Kray twins and I really like the  fact that helgeland drops us right in  the middle of the query story in 1960s  London so we avoid all the usual  childhood scenes and their rise to power  what we get instead is more the  expansion of their power from the east  to the West End and beyond their  aspirations of expanding their empire  still further and of course the events  that led to their eventual downfall and  I also like the way that gangster Jack  the Hat McVitie keeps popping up as a  thorn in the quayside throughout the  film after were introduced to him early  on in legends combo of seemingly  glamorous lifestyle and very unglamorous  violence he'll Berlin has gone for the  feel of a British Martin Scorsese movie  mixed with some of the movies scandal  about the Profumo affair  cares obviously been taken over dressing  both the actors and the sets giving the  film a glossy period  Sheen and plenty of dark humors also  been worked into the storyline too  however there are things though that  aren't really clear or at least seemed  out of place or disjointed in the script  like why does Ronnie seem to be living  in an old beat-up caravan in the woods  at one point also throughout the film we  hear voiceover narration from Francis I  wasn't keen on this framing device as it  seems incongruous given that she wasn't  involved in any way in so many of the  events that she narrates and her  character also ends up feeling more of a  means to an end than a fully written  fleshed out character still it's  interesting that the 1990 film the craze  and this film both find their way into  the brothers story via the women in  their life in the 1990 film the focus  was very much on them the violet whereas  in this latest film violet plays a very  small part and it's Francis who becomes  our guide still I much prefer helgeland  take on the craze to the 1990 film  starring Spandau Ballet brothers Martin  and Gary Kemp for me that whole film  felt melodramatic and really laid on the  symbolism way too thick so to sum up  although legend tells a familiar story  that's been told time and again in print  and on screen over the years writer  director brian helgeland has still  managed to make two hours and ten  minutes of compelling drama of course a  large part of that success is due to Tom  Hardy who puts in a remarkable  performance or rather two remarkable  performances and is a Blee supported by  a talented cast of well-known faces  legend gets three and a half out of 5  flicks now what do you think of legend  and what are your favorite gangster  flicks let me know in the comments below  as ever if you liked this video do  please share it hit the thumbs-up button  and subscribe for my movie reviews and  interviews thanks for watching and see  you next time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers  you
 

